",,True,-1,"The theorem is about whether the maximum of two elements is less than or equal to another element if and only if each of the two elements is less than or equal to that element. The theorem follows from a general property of the supremum.

To prove this theorem, I use the `sup_le_iff` lemma, which already defines this property. By applying this lemma, I can directly show that `max a b ≤ c ↔ a ≤ c ∧ b ≤ c`.

The classical case is handled by `Nat.mk_sup_le` in the `sup_le_iff` lemma. The nonclassical case is automatically handled using `LC_prop` of `Nat.le_antisymm`.

